111 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (The PortSwigger Web Security Academy Lab Project was conducted to gain practical experience in identifying and exploiting common web application security vulnerabilities in a controlled and legally authorized environment. The Web Security Academy provides interactive labs containing deliberately vulnerable web applications that allow students to practice real-world web security testing techniques.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
112 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (As part of this project, five Apprentice-level labs were successfully completed. The selected labs covered different vulnerability classes, including SQL Injection, Cross-Site Scripting \(XSS\), Broken Access Control, and File Path Traversal.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
113 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (The practical exercises involved analyzing application behavior, identifying vulnerable input points, crafting appropriate test payloads, using Burp Suite for HTTP request analysis and modification, and verifying the impact of each vulnerability. The project also focused on understanding appropriate defensive measures that can be implemented to prevent similar vulnerabilities in real-world applications.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
